  "notes": "xView (Lam et al. 2018): 10 vessel types (maritime vessel, motorboat, sailboat, tugboat, barge, fishing vessel, ferry, yacht, container ship, oil tanker). One chip per labelled vessel, cut with a context window of 3.5x the box (at least 160 px before resizing), long side resized to 448-640 px. Every box of the 10 classes with at least half of its area inside a chip is labelled. 261 of 5141 boxes whose coordinates overshoot their tile by more than 2 px are dropped. RandomState(2026).permutation per class on the sorted image keys; the first 12 go to eval, the next 88 at most to train_pool. No tile is shared between train and eval; yacht has only 5 train chips. Box ground truth only: each segmentation is the box as a rectangle polygon (box IoU convention). The chips are built from the xView tiles with build_xview_ships10.py."
}
